WEBVTT

00:02:30.710 --> 00:02:31.780
Why?

00:02:32.230 --> 00:02:34.490
Why can't I get him out of my head?

00:02:44.270 --> 00:02:45.680
What is this?

00:02:46.050 --> 00:02:50.970
Especially for you, Teppei-sama, Arima Manufacturing Automotive Research Department has built a high-tech bike.

00:02:51.310 --> 00:02:55.280
Yeah!  We heard Teppei-sama was looking for a bike that wouldn't fall over.

00:02:55.660 --> 00:02:58.770
The Research Lab put all its effort into building this.

00:02:59.180 --> 00:03:02.410
A bike that doesn't fall...  Did I ever say that?

00:03:03.820 --> 00:03:07.730
Then, would a motorbike that can't fall work?

00:03:07.730 --> 00:03:10.700
With Grandfather's resources, I'm sure someone could create something like that.

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:13.190
That's possible.

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:15.500
Have you recalled?

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:18.540
"That's possible," wasn't just you putting me off?

00:03:18.950 --> 00:03:23.150
Would I put off anything Teppei-sama says?

00:03:23.150 --> 00:03:24.570
No, I would never do that!

00:03:25.020 --> 00:03:26.410
Oh, the irony...

00:03:27.970 --> 00:03:29.430
Are you sure it can't fall?

00:03:29.430 --> 00:03:33.070
Of course, because it's full of the awesome power of Arima!

00:03:33.070 --> 00:03:36.180
Just try to kick it from this position to check it out.

00:03:36.590 --> 00:03:37.650
Like this?

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:38.360
Yes!

00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:46.120
It feels kind of unpleasant, so take it back!

00:03:51.690 --> 00:03:53.820
Hey Teppei, did you think of something?

00:03:54.230 --> 00:03:55.400
Nope.

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:58.190
Well, I almost never go to parties.

00:03:58.580 --> 00:04:01.710
I have absolutely no idea how to host a party myself.

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:05.630
You never attended any parties before you came here?

00:04:05.630 --> 00:04:10.050
Well, I did go to birthday and Christmas parties.

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:11.720
Those are great!

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:15.690
Well, it's completely different from what both of you would imagine it to be...

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:17.340
What, how would it be different?

00:04:18.210 --> 00:04:20.700
It's completely different in every way!

00:04:20.700 --> 00:04:24.880
Come to think of it, Seika-san hasn't been around for a while.

00:04:24.880 --> 00:04:27.320
Isn't that a little easygoing for the club president?

00:04:27.320 --> 00:04:30.820
You're not even a member, I don't want to hear you gossiping about the club president!

00:04:31.220 --> 00:04:33.070
Do you understand, you pig?

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:34.820
P-Pig?

00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:39.820
Seika-sama is the only daughter of the Outedari Jewelers,

00:04:39.820 --> 00:04:43.830
and Wakate Number One Designer House's model.

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:45.750
No way, is that true!?

00:04:45.750 --> 00:04:47.030
You didn't know?

00:04:47.030 --> 00:04:49.270
Everyone talks about her all the time.

00:04:49.270 --> 00:04:50.760
Ah, I heard about that!

00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:52.010
They usually talk about Houjouin.

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:54.400
Really?  I didn't know.

00:04:54.820 --> 00:04:57.290
She's an amazing person, huh?

00:04:57.700 --> 00:04:59.760
She could brag about herself as much as she wants.

00:05:00.100 --> 00:05:04.140
Don't you dare speak of her like that!

00:05:04.140 --> 00:05:07.320
That's right!  That's what I like about Seika-san!

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:08.810
I must admit, they're right.

00:05:09.210 --> 00:05:10.570
True.

00:05:10.570 --> 00:05:13.700
Well, if her loudmouth side wasn't there, I'd respect her more.

00:05:13.700 --> 00:05:14.990
What did you say!?

00:05:15.520 --> 00:05:18.900
Stop saying whatever you want when I'm not around!

00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:19.850
Mezu!

00:05:19.850 --> 00:05:20.910
Yes, I am here.

00:05:21.950 --> 00:05:23.200
I'm counting on you tomorrow.

00:05:23.620 --> 00:05:25.750
It is an honor to wait on you.

00:05:25.750 --> 00:05:29.170
You, the club president, are like the stars that guide me...

00:05:29.170 --> 00:05:34.030
Sheesh.  I can't believe the boys recruited into the club are all like this.

00:05:34.030 --> 00:05:35.790
You are being dishonest with yourself.

00:05:36.380 --> 00:05:39.050
It looks like you are the stereotypical AB blood type girl...

00:05:36.380 --> 00:05:39.050
Note: In Japan, girls with blood type AB are considered to be both shy and outgoing, commonly known as "loose cannons".

00:05:39.220 --> 00:05:41.250
<i>If you dare to say that sort of thing in front of the camera,</i>

00:05:41.250 --> 00:05:44.400
<i>I'll dump the entire program on you, so be prepared!</i>

00:05:45.060 --> 00:05:46.940
What are you looking at, Arima?

00:05:46.940 --> 00:05:49.120
No...I'm not looking at anything.

00:05:49.570 --> 00:05:53.330
Too bad, but I'm not going to leave anything up to you.

00:05:53.330 --> 00:05:54.820
I just don't understand you.

00:05:55.450 --> 00:05:59.010
Why should I answer to you about everything I do?

00:05:59.010 --> 00:06:01.500
Why is she always complaining about the tiniest things?

00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:02.640
Yeah, that's right.

00:06:02.640 --> 00:06:03.880
Absolutely.

00:06:04.580 --> 00:06:12.790
Actually, I'll be at the Hotel El-Grande participating at the Saint Rose Brand's newest product exhibition, as requested by---

00:06:15.450 --> 00:06:18.980
You make it sound as if I wanted to be the model.

00:06:18.980 --> 00:06:19.950
Oh, that's not it?

00:06:19.950 --> 00:06:20.390
That's not it!

00:06:21.350 --> 00:06:24.650
After the exhibition, there's going to be an interview.

00:06:25.050 --> 00:06:29.100
They want to hear about my high school life from a school friend.

00:06:29.840 --> 00:06:31.130
School friend...

00:06:31.130 --> 00:06:32.070
...and this guy is your---

00:06:32.070 --> 00:06:33.320
<i>I had no choice!</i>

00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:36.700
And if the representative requests this, I have no objections.

00:06:36.700 --> 00:06:41.570
Since it's the gala occasion of a lifetime, you will experience the utmost service from Mezu Haruhiko!

00:06:42.820 --> 00:06:47.030
I'll give you some of my anticipated questions and answers later.  Make sure you cram them into your head.

00:06:47.030 --> 00:06:49.180
There is no need to worry about that!

00:06:49.180 --> 00:06:50.080
I, Mezu Haruhiko---

00:06:52.320 --> 00:06:53.780
I am not <i>worried.</i>

00:06:53.780 --> 00:06:55.090
I'm saying that it's for my sake!

00:06:56.630 --> 00:06:57.270
<i>Stop laughing!</i>

00:06:57.270 --> 00:06:58.840
Sorry!

00:07:01.790 --> 00:07:06.620
I wonder why Seika-san keeps treating me like an enemy...

00:07:06.620 --> 00:07:09.040
You're being treated like an enemy?

00:07:09.530 --> 00:07:11.740
I don't really see that happening.

00:07:11.740 --> 00:07:13.270
But you know...

00:07:14.230 --> 00:07:18.990
...aside from me, I wonder if she's treating the entire Arima family like an enemy.

00:07:19.670 --> 00:07:20.910
Why do you think that is?

00:07:20.910 --> 00:07:22.820
I don't think I am qualified to say anything,

00:07:23.390 --> 00:07:26.990
I believe asking milord directly would be for the best.

00:07:27.300 --> 00:07:28.450
Grandfather?

00:07:28.450 --> 00:07:29.210
Yes.

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:32.420
I wonder if I can go now.

00:07:33.340 --> 00:07:35.840
Well, if that is your wish...

00:07:38.570 --> 00:07:40.380
Please bring me to where Grandfather is.

00:07:40.970 --> 00:07:41.980
Very well.

00:07:47.490 --> 00:07:49.330
How is school?

00:07:49.330 --> 00:07:50.850
Are you doing well?

00:07:51.320 --> 00:07:54.060
I don't really know if I'm doing well or not.

00:07:54.060 --> 00:07:55.900
But I'll get there gradually.

00:07:56.300 --> 00:07:57.230
I see.

00:07:59.050 --> 00:08:02.020
How is Van Hossen's daughter?

00:08:02.020 --> 00:08:02.950
She is a good girl isn't she?

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:04.110
Silvie?

00:08:04.110 --> 00:08:07.120
Well, we aren't really acting like fiancées or anything.

00:08:07.120 --> 00:08:08.980
But we're pretty good friends.

00:08:10.560 --> 00:08:12.480
Friends, eh?

00:08:12.540 --> 00:08:14.180
Sounds like you are doing splendidly.

00:08:14.180 --> 00:08:15.170
Guess so.

00:08:15.170 --> 00:08:16.210
I'll do it at my own pace.

00:08:16.680 --> 00:08:19.060
So, what was it that you wanted to talk about?

00:08:19.940 --> 00:08:24.040
You didn't come all the way out here to chit-chat, did you?

00:08:25.070 --> 00:08:27.500
There's this girl named Houjouin Seika.

00:08:28.090 --> 00:08:28.720
Do you know her?

00:08:29.810 --> 00:08:31.300
Houjouin?

00:08:42.670 --> 00:08:43.520
Teppei-sama?

00:08:45.480 --> 00:08:48.810
This has just arrived.  Is this okay with you?

00:08:48.810 --> 00:08:49.700
Thank you.

00:08:53.180 --> 00:08:54.990
I can't believe they're quarreling over just <i>that</i>...

00:08:55.450 --> 00:08:57.310
How am I supposed to show it to her, anyway?

00:09:00.590 --> 00:09:05.430
Excuse me, but this morning was particularly cold.

00:09:10.350 --> 00:09:12.350
I was supposed to go to the doctor...

00:09:12.990 --> 00:09:15.840
Well, your nose doesn't look well.

00:09:15.840 --> 00:09:17.550
No way!

00:09:17.890 --> 00:09:20.020
Did you...catch a cold?

00:09:21.180 --> 00:09:24.120
Someone like me, catching a cold?  Are you joking?

00:09:24.120 --> 00:09:27.880
Last night I was up a little late memorizing things...

00:09:27.880 --> 00:09:30.940
But the things weren't sinking in.

00:09:31.100 --> 00:09:32.080
I don't think it was just "a little" late.

00:09:32.870 --> 00:09:34.870
Fear not!

00:09:34.870 --> 00:09:38.980
Today, I, Mezu Haruhiko, will put all my effort into...

00:09:43.730 --> 00:09:45.740
I think I saw blood come out...

00:09:48.410 --> 00:09:50.480
The things that the captain said...

00:09:50.480 --> 00:09:52.720
...I will fill the star spangled banner in front of Arima...

00:09:53.340 --> 00:09:55.320
Teppei-sama, I'm scared!

00:09:56.090 --> 00:09:57.580
I think I'm going to get a fever, too!

00:10:02.810 --> 00:10:05.240
Ah.  School's over.

00:10:05.680 --> 00:10:07.810
Today passed so quickly!

00:10:08.020 --> 00:10:09.630
Well, you <i>were</i> sleeping the whole day.

00:10:11.300 --> 00:10:13.770
Well, I should go now.

00:10:15.680 --> 00:10:18.180
Hey, are you sure you can make it to the meeting place?

00:10:18.510 --> 00:10:22.010
Oh, so it's that time already.  Roger that!

00:10:22.510 --> 00:10:26.440
The president is a diligent person and is popular among the entire student body!

00:10:26.440 --> 00:10:29.700
She's like an angel that dances to the sound of the strings.

00:10:29.700 --> 00:10:32.000
Well, the interview hasn't started yet.

00:10:33.200 --> 00:10:39.980
When I looked at her official homepage profile, I was struck by the shock of her fame.

00:10:39.980 --> 00:10:46.450
Born with the rare AB-blood type, our leader, the representative, shall guide the club.

00:10:46.450 --> 00:10:50.620
The representative will, without fail, ensure the future of the...

00:10:59.090 --> 00:11:00.980
Why did this happen...?

00:11:01.600 --> 00:11:04.710
Well, it's my chance to show her this, anyway.

00:11:14.110 --> 00:11:19.930
Everyone, thank you for coming to Saint Rose's latest product exhibition.

00:11:20.990 --> 00:11:22.850
This season's masterpiece has finally been put together.

00:11:23.450 --> 00:11:28.150
We, the Saint Rose girls, call it "Spring"!

00:11:28.690 --> 00:11:31.570
Now, let us feast our eyes on the clothes of...

00:11:35.070 --> 00:11:35.780
Arima!?

00:11:38.560 --> 00:11:42.000
A-Anyway everyone, please look forward to the show!

00:11:43.330 --> 00:11:44.630
Why are you here, anyway!?

00:11:45.070 --> 00:11:46.750
Well, Mezu-kun is...err...

00:11:46.750 --> 00:11:48.520
...he caught a fever and is in a sickbed now.

00:11:48.530 --> 00:11:49.420
<i>Fever...</i>

00:11:49.870 --> 00:11:53.010
I didn't have time to find a replacement,

00:11:53.010 --> 00:11:54.760
so I had no choice but to become his stand-in!

00:11:56.880 --> 00:11:59.840
Houjouin-san, it's time to get on the stage.

00:11:59.840 --> 00:12:03.350
It can't be helped.  You'll replace Mezu.

00:12:03.800 --> 00:12:06.420
That's fine, but what should I say?

00:12:06.420 --> 00:12:07.560
Houjouin-san...

00:12:07.560 --> 00:12:08.440
I'm coming!

00:12:08.860 --> 00:12:10.150
There's no time to think about it now.

00:12:10.880 --> 00:12:11.990
I'll leave it to you.

00:12:11.990 --> 00:12:14.800
If you do anything horrible, I won't let it go.

00:12:14.800 --> 00:12:16.430
What do you mean by, "do anything horrible"...?

00:12:16.430 --> 00:12:17.290
Houjouin-san...

00:12:17.290 --> 00:12:19.450
I know, I'm going to change now!

00:12:27.090 --> 00:12:28.520
I'm sorry!

00:13:03.490 --> 00:13:04.810
Sorry for making you wait.

00:13:05.750 --> 00:13:08.910
We apologize for forcing this into your tight schedule.

00:13:08.910 --> 00:13:11.420
The readers have been anticipating this.

00:13:12.780 --> 00:13:17.220
It was difficult for Jonjon-san to take up this special interview, therefore he couldn't make it.

00:13:17.690 --> 00:13:24.450
Being able to interview you right after the exhibition is wonderful enough.

00:13:24.450 --> 00:13:27.190
Excuse me, can I have a picture?

00:13:27.990 --> 00:13:28.800
Sure!

00:13:34.540 --> 00:13:37.360
I think you've got an insect or something on your camera.

00:13:42.570 --> 00:13:47.600
I'm sorry.  Arima-san isn't used to these sorts of things yet.

00:13:47.600 --> 00:13:48.880
It's okay, neither am I.

00:13:49.240 --> 00:13:52.980
Arima-san, please excuse us for asking too much.

00:13:53.840 --> 00:13:55.880
It's okay.  Yes, no problem.

00:13:56.320 --> 00:13:59.860
Alright, then let us start with our interview.

00:13:59.860 --> 00:14:01.140
Um, Arima-san.

00:14:01.470 --> 00:14:02.480
Yes!

00:14:02.480 --> 00:14:07.420
Houjouin-san is working as the representative of Shuuhou Academy's Social Club,

00:14:07.420 --> 00:14:09.440
a society with a long tradition, is that right?

00:14:09.440 --> 00:14:10.440
Uh, yes.

00:14:13.810 --> 00:14:16.470
<i>Yes!</i>  And she's a good one at that.

00:14:16.470 --> 00:14:17.700
Ah, you flatter me.

00:14:18.650 --> 00:14:19.950
When are you going to stop messing with me?!

00:14:20.420 --> 00:14:24.140
Arima-san is also a member of the Social Club too, right?

00:14:24.140 --> 00:14:29.540
Huh?  Uh, well...me, I...no, not really.

00:14:30.510 --> 00:14:33.000
I haven't gotten Seika-san's approval yet.

00:14:34.250 --> 00:14:35.230
No way!

00:14:35.230 --> 00:14:39.510
That sounds like I'm the one refusing Arima-san!

00:14:39.990 --> 00:14:43.760
But, to us and our readers, you seem very close.

00:14:44.220 --> 00:14:46.890
What kind of activities does the Social Club hold?

00:14:47.690 --> 00:14:50.180
Ah.  The Social Club is, well...

00:14:51.470 --> 00:14:56.070
We, as the representatives of the students, constantly hold events in the school.

00:14:56.550 --> 00:15:02.320
Sometimes we also act as the voice of the students, and pass on the concerns of the students to the teachers.

00:15:02.800 --> 00:15:05.010
Like a student council?

00:15:05.020 --> 00:15:09.030
No, the Social Club does not hold any power in student affairs.

00:15:09.030 --> 00:15:11.920
Just think of it as us helping out with simple things.

00:15:12.300 --> 00:15:13.770
I see.

00:15:13.770 --> 00:15:14.840
So, Arima-san.

00:15:15.250 --> 00:15:19.830
What is your impression of Houjouin-san in your school life?

00:15:20.390 --> 00:15:22.090
Impression, eh?

00:15:23.820 --> 00:15:26.420
Well, besides the activities of the Social Club,

00:15:26.420 --> 00:15:29.810
there must be other ways that you two interact.

00:15:29.810 --> 00:15:32.520
Given that, could you please tell us more about her?

00:15:32.920 --> 00:15:34.970
That's...right.

00:15:34.970 --> 00:15:36.020
Seika-san is...

00:15:36.360 --> 00:15:40.060
the type that would say, "Shut up and follow me."

00:15:41.510 --> 00:15:43.620
No, it's nothing!

00:15:45.620 --> 00:15:47.050
Eh, well...

00:15:48.600 --> 00:15:51.370
So, do you both feel forced when you are together?

00:15:51.710 --> 00:15:52.680
Sometimes,

00:15:52.680 --> 00:15:56.240
she just gets too lively and you often get to see her being pushy.

00:15:57.210 --> 00:16:02.500
However, my impressions of Seika-san are...

00:16:02.500 --> 00:16:06.100
Seika-san is a very responsible and very earnest person.

00:16:07.690 --> 00:16:12.350
She doesn't think about her own loss or gain, but rather how to fulfill her responsibilities.

00:16:13.430 --> 00:16:15.360
People don't say, "come follow me" very often, right?

00:16:16.260 --> 00:16:18.390
But Seika-san says it often.

00:16:18.390 --> 00:16:22.110
That's because she is confident that she is walking down the right path.

00:16:22.930 --> 00:16:26.240
And she has the ability to notice the talents of people around her.

00:16:27.280 --> 00:16:30.390
She's both a student and a designer at the same time,

00:16:30.390 --> 00:16:33.000
but she isn't boastful at all.

00:16:49.750 --> 00:16:51.090
You were horrible.

00:16:51.090 --> 00:16:53.340
All the questions were unbelievably easy,

00:16:53.340 --> 00:16:56.310
but you ended up failing most of them.

00:16:56.910 --> 00:16:58.380
Well, sorry.

00:17:00.850 --> 00:17:03.460
What's wrong?  Lost your appetite?

00:17:04.290 --> 00:17:05.610
I heard the story.

00:17:05.610 --> 00:17:06.280
The story?

00:17:06.920 --> 00:17:10.050
Why you hate the Arima family so much.

00:17:10.050 --> 00:17:11.040
The reason for that.

00:17:15.070 --> 00:17:19.170
The founder of the Houjouin family's advertising company...

00:17:19.780 --> 00:17:24.920
...was originally running the Arima Financial Center's Personal Image Department.

00:17:26.290 --> 00:17:32.800
During the rapid growth after World War Two, Grandfather never went home and worked nonstop every day.

00:17:32.800 --> 00:17:36.010
His wife was feeling lonely from being left by herself.

00:17:36.720 --> 00:17:40.820
So she got into an affair with Seika's grandfather.

00:17:41.900 --> 00:17:45.320
When Grandfather found out, he expelled her from the Arima family.

00:17:46.130 --> 00:17:50.320
So the relationship between the two families started to drift apart.

00:17:50.760 --> 00:17:51.960
I know.

00:17:51.960 --> 00:17:53.980
It's a horrible story.

00:17:54.500 --> 00:17:56.210
So why are you going on about it now?

00:17:56.930 --> 00:18:00.460
It's about your brands being put on display at the Arima Department Stores.

00:18:01.350 --> 00:18:03.320
And about how they were completely revoked.

00:18:03.790 --> 00:18:06.340
It's just your grandfather interfering with things.

00:18:06.780 --> 00:18:09.140
So what if his daughter was running a shop by herself?

00:18:09.520 --> 00:18:12.260
The Arima Department Store was losing its dignity!

00:18:12.970 --> 00:18:16.830
Even without all those big businesses, the newspapers were already picking up on his deception!

00:18:25.750 --> 00:18:30.110
How long do you Arimas plan to keep up the hatred between us?

00:18:30.510 --> 00:18:33.370
Come to think of it, it's the fault of you and your grandfather!

00:18:33.960 --> 00:18:36.870
I only speak with hostility to my enemies.

00:18:37.540 --> 00:18:41.880
If you follow in the footsteps of that grandfather of yours, you'll end up in an even worse situation!

00:18:42.310 --> 00:18:43.960
Is that what you really think?

00:18:44.330 --> 00:18:45.360
It is.

00:18:45.920 --> 00:18:48.390
Look at it from my family's viewpoint.

00:18:48.390 --> 00:18:51.770
I will never bow to your grandfather!

00:18:56.990 --> 00:18:57.890
What is that?

00:18:59.160 --> 00:19:00.690
I want you to read it.

00:19:07.110 --> 00:19:07.860
Advisor...

00:19:08.160 --> 00:19:09.510
Arima Teppei?

00:19:10.130 --> 00:19:11.960
I convinced Grandfather to do it yesterday.

00:19:11.960 --> 00:19:13.980
It came into effect this morning.

00:19:14.510 --> 00:19:16.080
What are you thinking?

00:19:17.110 --> 00:19:22.030
Grandfather regrets what he did to <i>your</i> grandfather.

00:19:22.030 --> 00:19:25.590
But because too much time has passed, it was impossible to apologize.

00:19:26.290 --> 00:19:32.870
So the easy way to return leadership to the financial center, would be to provide stock to all members of the group.

00:19:33.730 --> 00:19:36.470
So, with our offer, can you please forgive us?

00:19:38.550 --> 00:19:44.330
After I heard about the old stories, I kept wondering if there was something I could do.

00:19:44.330 --> 00:19:46.900
It's because I felt bad about it,

00:19:46.900 --> 00:19:50.560
for being hated by Seika-san for something I didn't know about.

00:19:51.120 --> 00:19:54.100
I don't know if I'm going to cause trouble to the people at the store.

00:19:55.470 --> 00:19:56.870
But, please...

00:19:57.810 --> 00:20:01.010
...please start your business in our department store again!

00:20:04.600 --> 00:20:05.710
You're such a fool.

00:20:06.600 --> 00:20:07.130
Alright!

00:20:07.620 --> 00:20:09.260
You said it!

00:20:09.510 --> 00:20:11.590
I'll take that as a tenancy agreement!

00:20:13.140 --> 00:20:14.840
I'll leave it to you, Mr. Director!

00:20:16.900 --> 00:20:17.720
Fine.

00:20:18.180 --> 00:20:22.000
And, don't think you're off the hook just because of this.

00:20:22.230 --> 00:20:24.980
This deal doesn't have any effect on your assignment to host a party.

00:20:25.250 --> 00:20:27.190
Damn.  I thought so.

00:20:27.490 --> 00:20:30.080
In the end, even with help from your grandfather,

00:20:30.080 --> 00:20:33.010
you still can't free yourself from the requirements for entering the club.

00:20:33.010 --> 00:20:34.530
Well, I guess not.

00:20:35.400 --> 00:20:39.450
In a week, I expect the doors to be opened to a wonderful party!

00:20:40.470 --> 00:20:41.820
Fine.

00:20:50.410 --> 00:20:52.000
Good work today.

00:20:52.000 --> 00:20:55.890
I thank you for coming to my assistance today.

00:21:04.610 --> 00:21:06.270
That's awesome, Teppei!

00:21:07.040 --> 00:21:09.310
I told you not to hug me all of a sudden!

00:21:09.310 --> 00:21:13.490
It was a bit heavy-handed, but I guess you have brought an end to a long period of contention.

00:21:14.150 --> 00:21:16.660
Well, I only came into this world by chance.

00:21:17.410 --> 00:21:22.390
But now I get the feeling there might be even better things I can do.

00:21:22.390 --> 00:21:23.620
That's right, Teppei!

00:21:24.240 --> 00:21:26.470
It's the feeling of achievement.

00:21:26.470 --> 00:21:28.840
But you still have to host a party, right?

00:21:28.840 --> 00:21:31.520
Ah, I guess so...

00:21:51.090 --> 00:21:52.300
There!

00:23:25.580 --> 00:23:26.740
Question!

00:23:26.920 --> 00:23:28.640
What do you mean by, "woohoo"?

00:23:30.380 --> 00:23:33.380
Um, what do you mean by, "woohoo"?

00:23:33.890 --> 00:23:35.310
Next time on Princess Lover!

00:23:35.310 --> 00:23:36.350
Sunset and Ferris Wheel.

00:23:36.330 --> 00:23:38.110
<i>Hey, so what does "woohoo" mean?!</i>
